The Wigley hull specifications are according to 

 "Experiments and Calculations on 4 Wigley Hull Forms in Head Waves"
  J.M.J. Journée, Delft University of Technology

\eta = (1-\zeta^2)(1-\xi^2)(1+a_2*\xi^2 + a_4*\xi^4) + \alpha*\zeta^2*(1-\zeta^8)(1-\xi^2)^4

The wigley hull in this folder has the following characteristics:

model name: type I
a_2   = 0.2
a_4   = 0
alpha = 1
L/B   = 2/0.3
L/T   = 2/0.125

NOTE: The grids are built for L = 2 m.

To generate the "sharp" grid run the scripts as:

$Overture/bin/rap rap_whole
$Overture/bin/mbuilder hype_whole
$Overture/bin/ogen overlap

To employ surface integration by triangulation, build the patches as:

./build_patches

and put the "patches" folder in your calculation directory.

The grid with "round" corners has been built by Matilde H. Andersen, and can be generated as

$Overture/bin/rap Wigley_rap
$Overture/bin/mbuilder Wigley_aft_hype
$Overture/bin/mbuilder Wigley_fore_hype
$Overture/bin/mbuilder Wigley_ms_hype
$Overture/bin/ogen Wigley_overlap
